;. /surface_investigation_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition surface_investigation
  ;= Investigate through declared native actions

    This example explicitly delegates interactive work to the shared provider.
    Bind provider to the raw /0x11/io/codex/surface_provider record. Bind sources
    to captured evidence. Edit the brief below to name the objects and actions
    the task requires, then publish and attach with the ordinary Nenex writer.

    The provider can inspect native records, reflect declared Goo actions and
    invoke those actions through shared admission. It uses the same tool calls
    as an investigation, without the separate chat UI or an external MCP loop.
    The selected provider carries namespace authority; the brief is task scope,
    not a security sandbox. Rejected results keep their hole and can be retried.

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Captured task evidence

    ;@ /flow/input provider
    ;= Explicit interactive provider capability

    ;@ /flow/step task ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/surface_task
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Build the task from this authored brief

    ;@ /flow/step investigated ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/interactive_requests
    ;@ /flow/bind tasks task
    ;@ /flow/bind provider provider
    ;= Delegate through the shared native request hand

    ;@ /flow/step report ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/report_pages
    ;@ /flow/bind responses investigated
    ;= Read the validated report

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages report
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Retain the report and its source evidence

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Guarded report publication

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses task
    ;= Surface investigation report
      Read the captured task evidence and inspect the native objects it names.
      Discover their declared actions. For this initial example, report the
      available actions and their required inputs without invoking mutations.
      Separate what you observed from what the task still needs. Include exact
      native addresses so another person can inspect the same objects.
